Z||000024||k2m4||09-11-2001||02:07 PM||||Well I live and New York and i have the pleasure of working for Governor Patakis TV agencies...New York Networks as a television engineer. As i sit here typing this i look up at the monitor wall staring at all, and i mean all the Satillite feeds coming through here to where ever, and its sickening and disturbing. Currently NY state is pretty much shut down. The capital here is erie! People are scared and its almost a ghost town. No cars on the road ...police everywhere. Its kind of crazy i cant explain the ominous feeling thats going on here! ...i dont know people but for some reason i feel really vulnerable right now!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Kerm<BR>86 2M4<BR>86 1/2 GT||||reg||9
Z||000025||Fformula88||09-11-2001||02:15 PM||||10:15 AM the Federal Building alarm goes off and a voice comes over the loudspeaker:  "Please evacuate the building immediately and as quickly as possible in an orderly manner.  Only take time to grab essential items only!"<P>We had been huddled around a radio listening to events and f-ing ran outta that building.  I'm not sure I like working in a Federal Building the last few years!<P>They have also closed off the section of thruway that goes past the Niagara Hydro-Electric power plant.  You cannot get near it.  The Peace Bridge has been closed down (its the main border crossing to Canada!).<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">   <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000026||fiero56||09-11-2001||02:23 PM||||Several city school systems are closing. Most extra cur activities are cancelled everywhere. WPAFB is on alert. All of my AF neighbors are home(all non-essentials get to leave). At work we evacuated this morning, I've been home since 11am. <P>A friend who works downtown and shares a block with a military building is in lockdown. They have military everywhere with automatic weapons, hummers etc. No-one is allowed to go anywhere, he is stuck at work, waiting to be allowed to leave.<P>Cops are out everywhere it seems, and people are suggested to avoid downtown if at all possible.||||reg||1
Z||000027||FieroLisa||09-11-2001||02:29 PM||||In Columbus, couple schools are shut down,there are canceling classes here at my school, airport is shut down as are city state and nat'l gov't buildings. I don't have class today and no car right now, been glued to the TV.||||reg||1
Z||000028||Sleeper||09-11-2001||02:37 PM||||in Los Angeles the police are on tachical alert and government, city buildings and malls, etc. are closed. also the border is closed too. and of course LAX is closed too.||||reg||1
Z||000029||Fiero5||09-11-2001||02:37 PM||||We had an emergency staff meeting at the High School here at about 11:am, and discussed the possibilty of closing the school for the rest of the day. We have some students that have relatives/friends either on one of the planes from Boston and work in one of the towers, etc. Two staff members both actually have sons that work in the trade center. One son finally was able to call his mother at home, who immediatly called the teacher here to let him know his son was oK. The son was running late and got stuck on the subway. If he had been on time, he very well would not be alive now. The second son was IN tower one when the plane hit the building. He grabbed his stuff and his laptop and got out of there. He was able to e-mail his girlfriend at their apartment to have her call his mother who works here.<BR>Anyway, all the staff was for closing the school for the rest of the day, as the kids are all distracted now anyway. BUT, we decided to keep them here as many have no rides home that don't use the bus system.<P>We are trying to keep things business as usual. It is pretty hard. <BR>Tons of students wanted to jump on the web to look up the latest, but the web sites were all tied up or the servers had crashed due to the large number of hits. I was able to get into the Associated Press web site system thru a back door, and loaded up a bunch of computers for the students in the computer lab.<BR>We (staff) have been told that we are going to have a quick staff meeting after school, to discuss how to handle the students and the questions for tomm.<BR>I am trying to set up a new LT server and full switch bank for "HALF" the school today. I can't get anything done as my "help" keeps wanting to go into the auditorium to watch the latest on the big screen.<P>Oh well, I guess I can't blame them.<P>Steve||||reg||1
Z||000030||DaRkLoRD||09-11-2001||02:58 PM||||I live in a fairly small town (12,000 people) and I've noticed extra police out today, but I'm not sure it's related at all, because they've just been stopping speeders..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>though since we do have a large portion of Ontario's power generating facilities here... it's not out of the question that security would be stepped up..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000031||fierobaby||09-11-2001||03:13 PM||||Berea Ohio-<P>if were wanted to and had a ride home we could leave school early... I live right by Hopkins Airport and as of about 20 minutes ago they were still going through that bomb plane... FAA has closed airports till at least noon tomorrow so looks like Scott is getting paid for not working again... I'm sure hes not complaining concidering he gets 3 almost 4 days in a row off... to bad it has to be because of this... I just wanted to say I am praying for all of you who know anyone who might be hurt.||||reg||1
Z||000032||GarethWright||09-11-2001||05:33 PM||||Tulsa /B.A. Oklahoma<BR>High Schools cancelled after school activity<BR>Colleges Closed (after my classes were done)<BR>Courts and most offices downtown closed and evacuated for the day<BR>Airport closed until tomorrow<BR>People beating each other up at the gas stations because of a price hike + shortage hoax<BR>||||reg||1
